From 92a7194587f9c2ba28ee9cadbb62d5eddbd60069 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Alexander=20Thei=C3=9Fen?= <alex@theissen.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:14:21 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Split x87 runs on pages that rewrite their code, and reuse
 target buffers (#54)

A run of x87 instructions is answered with one reply, so the instruction
map has no entry between a store and the instructions after it. When
the store patched a later instruction of the same run, the runtime
finished the translation to the run's end after the write fault, and
the old instruction ran once more. Separately, every translation whose
output did not fit the target's buffers allocated a new target region
that was never freed.

## Changes

- On a page whose maximum protection allows writing and on which a
  block came back from the same start with different bytes over the
  range both versions cover, a run ends after every x87 store to guest
  memory, with no bridging or fusion across it. Every wine PE image has
  a writable maximum protection, and Rosetta retranslates unchanged
  code at 4 KB block boundaries, so both conditions are needed.
- `X87_SMC_SPLIT=0` turns the split off, `=2` applies it to every
  block. The throughput and idle lines report `smc_pages`.
- Each grown target buffer (instruction buffer, `_fixups`,
  `external_fixups`) has a pool of at most two regions, reused once the
  TR read at the start of a request no longer points to one. Stock runs
  one translation at a time under a global lock and reaches these
  buffers only through the TR.
- A list placed in a sidecar region gets an `end_cap` that is a whole
  number of 12-byte entries. The page-rounded one let stock's push fast
  path write entry 342 past the region and crash the target.

## Validation

- `test_x87_smc`: the same-run patch cases fail 499 or 500 of 500
  (`patch_len` 250) before and pass after; stock passes. Never-written
  code crossing 4 KB on a file mapping keeps the code it emits with
  `X87_SMC_SPLIT=0`.
- `test_x87_retranslate_mem`: +8,192,000 bytes per 2000 retranslations
  before, +0 after; the 342-fixup cases exit 139 before and pass after.
- `run_tests.sh` on macOS 27.2.1: 1577 passed, 0 failed. CI passes on
  macOS 15, 26 and 27.
- Emitted code on r-x image pages is unchanged; benchmark geometric
  mean 1.001 against master.

## Not covered

- No run under wine.
- The first execution that rewrites a page still runs the old
  instruction once. #53 rounds some int64 copies on marked pages.

Closes #52

